---
// "Why mushrooms?" story with the interactive mushroom. Shared by the home and About pages.
import MushroomBuddy from './MushroomBuddy.astro';

interface Props {
  class?: string;
}
const { class: className } = Astro.props;
---
<section class:list={['section', className]} id="mushrooms">
  <div class="wrap mush">
    <div class="buddy-wrap"><MushroomBuddy size={240} /></div>
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">A small obsession</span>
      <h2>Why mushrooms?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        If you've spotted little mushrooms growing all over this site, that's no accident. I'm a bit obsessed with them.
      </p>
      <p>
        There's something magical about the way mushrooms grow. They don't wait for perfect conditions. They push up
        through the dark, in damp corners and on fallen wood, in places where almost nothing else can survive. They
        ask for very little care, and yet they grow into something beautiful and genuinely useful: they feed us, heal
        us and bring the forest floor back to life.
      </p>
      <p>
        I relate to that. I don't need perfect conditions to grow either. Give me a difficult environment, a little
        room and some time, and I'll find a way to turn it into something beautiful and useful.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mush { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr; gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px); align-items: center; }
  .mush p:not(.lede) { color: var(--muted); }
  .buddy-wrap { display: flex; justify-content: center; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .mush { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
